  "notes": "{膨|ふく}らます means to cause something to expand, inflate, or swell. Used both literally (balloons, cheeks) and figuratively (imagination, expectations).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {膨|ふく}らむ (intransitive — to swell on its own)\n- Pattern: Xを{膨|ふく}らます\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {膨|ふく}らませている: is in the process of inflating (ongoing action)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {風船|ふうせん}を{膨|ふく}らます: to inflate a balloon\n- {頬|ほほ}を{膨|ふく}らます: to puff out one's cheeks (often showing displeasure)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {想像|そうぞう}を{膨|ふく}らませる: to let one's imagination run wild\n- {期待|きたい}を{膨|ふく}らませる: to raise one's expectations/hopes\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{膨|ふく}らませる: to expand one's dreams",
